<h2>Whole finger vs. split vs. powder</h2>
<p>Form is usually the first decision on a turmeric order — it affects shelf life, storage risk and how much control you keep over final grinding quality. Whole finger and split turmeric retain quality longest and suit buyers with their own grinding capability; powder is convenient for direct use but has a materially shorter shelf life once ground, since grinding exposes more surface area to oxidation. Match the form to your processing setup and turnover speed rather than defaulting to powder for convenience alone.</p>
